.TH "ZYPPER-DECLARATIVE" "1" "May 2026" "zypper-declarative 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
zypper-declarative - declarative, reconciling converger surfaced as a
zypper subcommand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]zypper declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] converges a SUSE system (SL Micro 6.2, SLES
16.1) to a desired manifest, inside a single snapshot transaction,
recording what was applied.
The manifest is the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery
system-description format (packages, repositories, services,
config_files), serialised as canonical JSON (\f[V]format_version\f[R] 1)
or, optionally, as YAML.
.PP
Options are \f[I]key=value\f[R] pairs and precede any bare-word
argument.
POSIX \f[V]--flag\f[R] style is not used, except as tolerated aliases
for the global commands \f[B]version\f[R] and \f[B]help\f[R].
Behaviour is never controlled by environment variables; use
\f[I]key=value\f[R] options or preset files.
.SH VERBS
.TP
\f[B]apply\f[R]
Converge the system to the desired manifest in one snapshot transaction.
Idempotent: a second run against an unchanged manifest and an undrifted
system makes no changes.
.TP
\f[B]diff\f[R]
Dry run.
Compute and print what \f[B]apply\f[R] would change, making no
modification and opening no transaction.
.TP
\f[B]verify\f[R]
Check whether the actual state equals the applied declaration, modulo
the keep-list.
Reads live state by default, or a supplied state dump.
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Print the current declarative state: the applied manifest hash, the
generation, the resolved package count, and a one-line drift summary.
.TP
\f[B]describe\f[R]
Read the actual state of the declarable scopes and emit it as a manifest
in the resolved serialisation (JSON by default, YAML on request).
.SH GLOBAL COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R]
Print the program name, version, and embedded spec hash to stdout; exit
0.
Tolerated alias: \f[V]--version\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]help\f[R]
Print usage to stdout; exit 0.
Tolerated aliases: \f[V]--help\f[R], \f[V]-h\f[R].
.PP
A bare invocation with no verb prints usage to stdout and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]mode=\f[R]auto|external|internal
Transaction binding; default auto.
.TP
\f[B]manifest-path=\f[R]*path*
Desired manifest; default from CONFIG.
.TP
\f[B]format=\f[R]json|yaml
Serialisation for this invocation\[cq]s manifest I/O.
When omitted, the operative file extension decides, else
\f[B]manifest-format\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]manifest-format=\f[R]json|yaml
Fallback serialisation; default json.
.TP
\f[B]state-path=\f[R]*path*
State dump used as the actual-state source for \f[B]verify\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]root=\f[R]*path*
Root to describe; default \[lq]/\[rq].
.TP
\f[B]out=\f[R]*path*
\f[B]describe\f[R] output file; default stdout.
.TP
\f[B]on-unreadable=\f[R]error|warn
For \f[B]describe\f[R]: fail (default) or omit+warn on an unreadable
source; never emit an empty scope.
.PP
Additional CONFIG knobs accepted as options: \f[B]repo-lock\f[R],
\f[B]content-store\f[R], \f[B]keep-list\f[R],
\f[B]signature-verification\f[R], \f[B]keyring\f[R],
\f[B]activation-policy\f[R], \f[B]applied-root\f[R].
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success: convergence complete or no-op, system matches declaration, or
describe produced output.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Logical failure: convergence failed and discarded; verify found drift;
manifest invalid, unsafe-YAML, or unverified; state collection failed.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Invocation error: bad arguments; unknown format value; manifest
unreadable; insufficient privilege; transaction mechanism unavailable;
output path unwritable; malformed state dump.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]/usr/lib/zypper-declarative/applied.json\f[R]
The applied record of a generation.
Always canonical JSON.
.TP
\f[I]/etc/zypp/repos.d/\f[R].repo*
The on-disk zypp repository configuration, read for the repositories
scope.
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
Install via the openSUSE Build Service (OBS):
\f[V]zypper install zypper-declarative\f[R] (or the distribution\[cq]s
\f[V]apt\f[R]/\f[V]dnf\f[R] equivalent).
curl-based installation is not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]zypper\f[R](8), \f[B]snapper\f[R](8),
\f[B]transactional-update\f[R](8), \f[B]systemctl\f[R](1)
.SH AUTHORS
Matthias G. Eckermann.
